Z||000000||gtsonly||05-27-2000||05:22 AM||||on my 86 gt i just found the egr tube, not just cracked, but completely broken from the bottom of the plenum. the car has been idling high for sometime. the car has been like this for some time and i have never gotten any lights or codes????? would this be??? i capped off the bottom of the plenum and the egr tube. I already know what you all are going to say, but is this ok? it is just emissions!!!!<BR>  your help would be great<BR>                 chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-27-2000||10:27 AM||||Just go to Mr. Pontiac and order a replacement tube. $70.  There are only four bolts holding it on.  Two are basically inaccessable unless you remove the distributor cap, and have some time.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||05-27-2000||01:06 PM||||i have one and it's in good shape, if you are interested and want to see it email me and i will send you a pic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||05-27-2000||01:57 PM||||Did somebody say "<I>Disconnected EGR?!!</I><P>I'm gonna go hide somewhere now. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||7
Z||000004||ezsurf||05-27-2000||07:02 PM||||I've read several articles that say if you cap off the EGR tube you will eventually burn the #2 and #5 pistons.  I repaired my EGR tube with some stuff I found a Wal Mart called Thermo Steel ($5.00).  It's good to 2400 deg F.  J & B Weld will not handle the heat (only 600 deg F).  Look into it before you block it off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-28-2000||07:00 AM||||IRM motorsports has a replacement EGR tube for V-6 only of flexible braided steel. Itll never break, comes with new gaskets for both ends flor $90. In Maryland (301) 948-3301||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||05-28-2000||08:16 PM||||Hey gtsonly! The offers still there if you want mine from my parts car. I'll give you a call this week and have you over. I've been looking forward to seeing your ride. Never seen t-top Fieros up close!||||reg||2
Z||000007||Denise||05-28-2000||08:48 PM||||Use Silver solder you can silver solder with a regular propane torch. the supplies are at Refrigeration supply houses. get silver wire and silver soder flux. it will work with less heat then brazing with brass. <BR>you must use the flux for it to stick there a diff kinds of flux for disimular metals like copper to brass brass to steel stainless too shold be able to be silver soldered.  mine hasn't cracked yet. one day it will I"m sure.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay||05-29-2000||07:32 PM||||I would recommend using the braided EGR tube.  As was mentioned it won't break because it can flex, and then you never have to worry about it again, at least not for a long time.  If you block it off, I'll call the mounties on you!!!||||reg||1
